======================================================================
FIX REQUEST (for custom-layout)
======================================================================
fix_request_id: sky130-pv-fr001
failure_class:  drc_lvs
route_to:       custom-layout
priority:       HIGH

Fix 1 (PRIMARY): Correct poly-diff overlap in all device cells.
  The poly gate must overlap the diffusion active region by the
  sky130 minimum poly enclosure of active = 0.13 um (26 magic units).
  Current: poly touches diff at boundary (0 overlap)
  Required: poly extends 0.13 um BEYOND each diff edge (source and drain)
  Impact: Will enable FET device extraction and resolve poly.4 DRC errors.
  Files: layout/scripts/02_cp_devices.tcl, 03_vco_devices.tcl,
         layout/mag/cp_pmos_array.mag, cp_nmos_array.mag,
         vco_stage_unit.mag, sky130_vco_layout.mag, sky130_bias_layout.mag

Fix 2: Correct minimum dimension violations.
  All geometry must meet sky130 minimum rules:
  - LI width >= 0.17 um (34 magic units at 1u=200 units)
  - LI spacing >= 0.17 um
  - Poly width >= 0.15 um
  - Diffusion width >= 0.15 um
  - Nwell must contain connected N+ tap (nwell.4)
  The scripted cells are drawing at 1-2 unit widths (5-10 nm) which
  are far below the 0.15-0.17 um minimums.

Fix 3: Scale calibration.
  Confirm that device W/L values in the .mag files correspond to the
  intended schematic dimensions (e.g. PMOS W=4u = 800 magic units
  at 1 magic unit = 0.005 um / 1 lambda = 0.1 um). The current
  geometry is ~10-50x too small.

