======================================================================
HONEST ASSESSMENT
======================================================================
The layout cells have the correct layer types and approximate
bounding-box geometry, but two fundamental problems prevent sign-off:
(1) Geometry dimensions are in incorrect scale / too small, triggering
    all minimum-width DRC rules.
(2) Poly-diff relationship is "touching" not "overlapping", preventing
    device extraction for LVS.

A real block-level LVS clean result (PASS) for CP and VCO cannot be
claimed for this iteration. The fix_request to custom-layout is
mandatory before re-attempting LVS.

The DRC sign-off score for the custom-layout stage's prior claim
of "DRC=0 per-cell" was incorrect; the real magic drc(full) shows
39 violations in the complete analog cells.
